# Everything else: see .env.advanced.example — you almost certainly don't need it.
#
# DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash on four CMP 170HX cards. ./start.sh copies this file to
# .env on first run and reads only .env. Every setting is commented out and
# shows its default; uncomment a line to change it, then run ./start.sh restart.
# One KEY=value per line; a value on the command line beats .env for that run:
#   PORT=8001 ./start.sh restart

# Listen address: 127.0.0.1 = this machine only; 0.0.0.0 = every interface (set API_KEY first).
# HOST=127.0.0.1

# API port.
# PORT=8000

# When set, every /v1 request must send "Authorization: Bearer <key>"; unset = no key.
# API_KEY=

# The model id clients send.
# SERVED_MODEL_NAME=dsv41-flash

# Where the checkpoints go (~680 GiB), one directory each; a relative path is
# taken from this checkout. Keep it on an SSD if the Engram tables are read
# from disk (below).
# MODELS_DIR=./models

# The Engram tables: ram = held in host RAM (~189 GiB; the server takes
# 202-204 GiB in all; the published numbers); ssd = read from the checkpoint
# files on disk, for hosts with less memory (slower).
# VLLM_ENGRAM_PLACEMENT=ram

# Peer access: auto verifies content before enabling P2P.
# off disables it; force bypasses verification. See docs/how-to-use.md.
# P2P=auto
